{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1198257-uncommon-plot-world-setup-and-ideas","id":1198257,"title":"Uncommon plot/world setup and ideas.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-21T23:17:47-07:00","id":1198257,"title":"Uncommon plot/world setup and ideas.","content":"So, I've had a few ideas after reading the WW2 first edition setting. I was wondering if anyone came up with some different worlds, rather than the standard Modern Era Scion game?<br /> <br /> I had two, One was a Post-Apoc world. Where the Titan's Influence slipped into the world for a bit after Pandora's box was opened. Then, the Titan energy started to make Titanspawn in an unchecked fashion. The WORLD found out about the Gods and everything else. Wars started, magic was used, Fate went wild, and in the final moments of the Last Titan War, Mankind witnessed what true power really was. The Gods have all but gone, hidden to lick their wounds, and bury their dead. Scions are still around, the Heroes and Demi-gods are alive. The young Gods died, using the last of their power to protect the world, Humans struggle to find some good land. Around the world many hard shifts of freak storms, sudden earthquakes, and various monsters or other supernatural things are happening. Then, Fate started to play around, making Scions appear and trying to balance the world again. Old Relics were being recovered, new ones were being made by Demi-Gods or Heroes, and each of them were trying to build the world again.<br /> <br /> One was simply a Wild West Era game. Some tweaking for some Boons to have some good flavor fit. It was later in the Era, so more tech was around and still left many unexplored places and plenty of hiding spots for Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> I did think of a Noir setting, but I never went anywhere with it. Could be interesting.... &quot;How does someone drown a Siren?&quot; Or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24011-ivoryknight22","name":"Ivoryknight22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T02:04:06-07:00","id":1198272,"title":"","content":"My last game was pretty much leading to the end of the World and Colonizing Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T06:37:12-07:00","id":1198309,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking on a game set in a giant hyper advanced colony-ship where the ships AI is a primordial with positive inclination towards humanity, the titans are the previous Crew that went mad with power (and maybe some sort of eldritch celestial corruption) and had to be imprisoned. The players would be people selected by the ship to become the Crew but have to be proven worthy.<br /> And that is all i have so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T08:35:09-07:00","id":1198331,"title":"","content":"my actual plot is this<br /> <br /> 1) A scion make a terrorist attack.<br /> 2) humans think that it's just a normal terroristic attack but not the high sphere of thw world<br /> 3) because of this explosion of divine power there is a new Divine Reinassance with the reawakening of the gods, new scion, monsters etcetc<br /> 4) meanwhile the a military unit raised by different government in the world is created, the W.O.L.F.<br /> 5) the witchhunt is begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T15:46:06-07:00","id":1198429,"title":"","content":"I have got a plot idea where the players are a group of Scions sharing a Brooklyn apartment building. It'll be a mostly character-based plot revolving around them learning about their powers and dealing with their parents.<br /> <br /> It's Girls meets American Gods, basically.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T16:17:44-07:00","id":1198446,"title":"","content":"So my current game is loosely based on Ducktales... except with a Investigating Detective, a Spy/assassin, a Singer and a Ice Artist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar324_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T16:22:23-07:00","id":1198447,"title":"","content":"Heavy. Metal. Road trip. The players are all in a band, traveling the country to win entry to a secret battle of the bands. The characters are all pre-visitation, and have no idea that the gods themselves will be at the show","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T16:38:53-07:00","id":1198453,"title":"","content":"I've been pondering the idea of Scions as public superheroes (and villains), drawing a bit on Green Ronin's Paragons setting for Mutants &amp; Masterminds and a long running superheroes setting idea I've had based on the sci-fi superhero shows of the 70s, 80s and early 90s (Six Million Dollar Man, Wonder Woman, Knight Rider, Mantis, etc.). <br /> <br /> Also, maybe some sort of alternate history thing set around the very early 20th century in a world were Andrew Jackson died at the Battle of New Orleans, resulting in a US that didn't remove the Native nations from the Southeast or fight the Mexican War, Florida is still a British colony/territory, the Republic of Texas was originally heavily settled by Bonapartist refugees, Alaska is still a Russian territory (destined to become the home of the Romanov dynasty in exile), and Hawaii is still an independent kingdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T17:43:36-07:00","id":1198466,"title":"","content":"In the same vein of superhero inspiration. I am trying to create a fictional city setting (kind of like Metropolis or Gotham). <br /> What i have so far is that it is renown as the city in north america that was the hotspot for immigration and multiculturalism (much in the way of Toronto and New York). It is also famous for the biggest amount of place of worship in a city (a bit in the manner of Montreal). For the name i'm thinking of going with the city of Pantheon.<br /> I like the idea of the city to be an interesting mishmash of various neighborhoods coexisting tenously together. You'd have chinatown beside little Ulster and little mumbai right next to ... midgardburg (i'm improvising the names). The point is to have elements of all the core pantheons coexisting within the same city.<br /> I'd also have to think of a concept for a thriving criminal underbelly of the city for the players to have something to face off against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T17:59:59-07:00","id":1198468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1198257-uncommon-plot-world-setup-and-ideas?p=1198466#post1198466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the same vein of superhero inspiration. I am trying to create a fictional city setting (kind of like Metropolis or Gotham).</div> </div> </div> </div>New Babylon?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:12:54-07:00","id":1198473,"title":"","content":"Could just be &quot;Babylon&quot; given how many cities in the US are named after foreign cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:41:04-07:00","id":1198493,"title":"","content":"Nothing too detailed yet, but my basic thought was post-apocalyptic, insofar as Titanomachy happened with the Titans on the winning end. The gods more or less survived, but have now more-or-less based on the moon and are running from a Titan-infested Earth, trying to find a way to consolidate power and take the world back. In the meantime, they're hunted by Coyolxauhqui because, y'know, they took the moon. Think the Lunar JRPG series meets Battlestar Galactica.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}